  "output": {
    "answer": "That's a simulated persona number, not a usability measurement — the panel walked a fixed-size browser, no human involved. And the record on this one cuts against trusting it: that same panel said DONE, and the next morning on my own phone it was pretty much unusable. So I treat panel numbers like Dez's as a proxy only, never a done signal by themselves. After that gate failed, I moved every labeler test to run at phone, tablet and desktop widths in a live browser, and a real-device walk became the last step before calling anything done.",
